1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,678
What if the world paused whenever you stopped moving?

2
00:00:03,718 --> 00:00:05,576
You're sprinting for the bus,

3
00:00:05,616 --> 00:00:07,278
you stop to tie your shoe,

4
00:00:07,318 --> 00:00:09,241
and everything stops with you.

5
00:00:09,281 --> 00:00:10,877
A bird hangs in mid-flap.

6
00:00:10,917 --> 00:00:12,775
A cyclist freezes mid-wobble.

7
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:15,329
At first it's a disaster,

8
00:00:15,369 --> 00:00:17,529
until you realize the best part:

9
00:00:17,569 --> 00:00:18,698
you can sit down,

10
00:00:18,738 --> 00:00:21,242
close your eyes, and take a nap while

11
00:00:21,282 --> 00:00:23,442
the entire world waits politely.

12
00:00:23,482 --> 00:00:26,261
Hypothetically, it's the best sleep ever.

13
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:28,503
Then the pranks begin.

14
00:00:28,543 --> 00:00:30,878
You wander through the frozen town,

15
00:00:30,918 --> 00:00:33,864
swapping hats, stacking cups into a tower on

16
00:00:33,904 --> 00:00:35,424
a sleeping chef's head,

17
00:00:35,464 --> 00:00:39,021
and adding a tiny moustache to a very serious statue.

18
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:41,194
But there's a problem.

19
00:00:41,234 --> 00:00:42,677
You can't stand still.

20
00:00:42,717 --> 00:00:45,712
Sneezing is dangerous, and being trapped in a

21
00:00:45,752 --> 00:00:47,196
long queue is torture,

22
00:00:47,236 --> 00:00:49,893
because the line only moves when you do.

23
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:51,849
So you start dancing in line.

24
00:00:53,150 --> 00:00:56,265
Scientists say time can't depend on one person's

25
00:00:56,305 --> 00:00:59,353
wiggling, so this is only a thought experiment.

26
00:00:59,393 --> 00:01:01,851
But it would make you the most fidgety

27
00:01:01,891 --> 00:01:05,334
person on Earth, and the world's strangest metronome.

28
00:01:05,850 --> 00:01:07,073
Here is the twist.

29
00:01:07,113 --> 00:01:09,740
One evening, you stop in the middle of

30
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:12,968
a frozen park, and somebody else keeps moving.

31
00:01:13,008 --> 00:01:15,214
A girl on a scooter glides past,

32
00:01:15,254 --> 00:01:17,390
whistling, completely unfrozen.

33
00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:18,653
She smiles at you.

34
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:22,205
She tells you she's been doing this for years.

35
00:01:22,245 --> 00:01:24,614
Two people, standing perfectly still,

36
00:01:24,654 --> 00:01:26,437
in a perfectly paused world,

37
00:01:26,477 --> 00:01:28,130
finally talking for hours.

38
00:01:28,170 --> 00:01:30,669
And outside, not one second has passed.

39
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:33,072
So the two of you stand up and

40
00:01:33,112 --> 00:01:35,624
start to dance through the paused city,

41
00:01:35,664 --> 00:01:38,502
past hanging confetti and floating balloons.

42
00:01:38,542 --> 00:01:39,941
When you finally stop,

43
00:01:39,981 --> 00:01:41,380
the world stays still,

44
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:42,950
as if politely clapping.
